# =====================================================================
# .gitignore – Credit Card Fraud Detection (Data Science coursework)
# Principle: ignore the dataset, secrets, caches and run-time artefacts;
# keep source code, tests, README and the reports that must be submitted.
# =====================================================================

# --- 1. Raw / processed data (never commit the Kaggle dataset) -------
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
# Safety net: the dataset must not be committed even if placed elsewhere.
creditcard*.csv
creditcardfraud*.zip

# --- 2. Secrets / credentials (Kaggle API token, env files) ----------
kaggle.json
.kaggle/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.pem
*.key
credentials*.json

# --- 3. Virtual environments -----------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- 4. Python / tool caches and build output ------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- 5. Trained models (can be large) --------------------------------
# Ignore everything in models/ except the placeholder and the small
# threshold metadata file. If the final selected model is small
# (check size first, e.g. < 50 MB) add it deliberately with:
#     git add -f models/best_model.joblib
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
!models/model_metadata.json
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.pickle

# --- 6. Files generated while running experiments --------------------
# outputs/ = scratch space (logs, intermediate predictions, ...).
# Figures/tables that go into the final report live in reports/ and
# ARE tracked.
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
*.log

# --- 7. Editor / OS noise --------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
